20: The processing status of each operation are saved into Chrom (7, :);
21: End For
22: For z = 1 to all-oper Do
23: Read genes in Chrom one by one from left to right;
24: If the current operation is the first operation of the jobs Then
25: The factory fa-rank with the shortest cumulative processing time was randomly selected from the available factories set avai-fa to process the current operation;
26: The workshop wo-rank with the shortest cumulative processing time was randomly selected from the available workshop set avai-wo to process the current operation;
27: The machine ma-rank with the shortest cumulative processing time was randomly selected from the available machine set avai-ma to process the current operation;
28: Record the processing time pro-time and processing cost pro-cost of this operation in the fa-rank, wo-rank and ma-fank;
29: Chrom (1:3, z) ← [fa-rank, wo-rank, ma-rank];
30: Chrom (5:6, z) ← [pro-time, pro-cost];
31: Else
32: [Pre-fa, Pre-wo, Pre-ma] ← [Chrom(1, z-1), Chrom(2, z-1), Chrom(3, z-1)];
33: If Pre-fa==avai-fa Then
34: If Pre-wo==avai-wo Then
35: If Pre-ma==avai-ma Then
36: ma-fank ← Pre-ma; wo-rank ← Pre-wo; fa-rank ← Pre-fa;
37: Else
38: Select an available machine ma1_rank from avai-ma at random;
39: ma-rank ← ma1_rank; wo-rank ← Pre-wo; fa-rank ← Pre-fa;
40: End If
41: Else
42: Select an available workshop wo1_rank from avai-wo at random;
43: Select an available machine ma1_rank from avai-ma at random;
44: ma-rank ← ma1_rank; wo-rank ← wo1_rank; fa-rank ← Pre-fa;
45: End If
46: Else
47: Select an available factory fa1_rank from avai-fa at random;
48: Select an available workshop wo1_rank from avai-wo at random;
49: Select an available machine ma1_rank from avai-ma at random;
50: ma-rank ← ma1_rank; wo-rank ← wo1_rank; fa-rank ← fa1_rank;
51: End If
52: Chrom (1:3, z) ← [fa-rank, wo-rank, ma-rank];
53: Chrom (5:6, z) ← [protime, procost];
54: End If
